e=1)\nciteturn26search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; 1972 Sep;2(3):132–135. doi: 10.1128/aac.2.3.132 ... Presented in part at the 11th Interscience Conference on Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy, Atlantic City, N.J., 19–22 October 1971. ... Cephamycin C was isolated from a different fermentation broth by ion-exchange and gel-filtration methods. ... 1971 May 5;93(9):2308–2310. doi: 10.1021/ja00738a035. ... [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n. 1972 Sep;2(3):132–135. doi: 10.1128/aac.2.3.132\n\n# Cephamycins, a New Family of β-Lactam Antibiotics II. Isolation and Chemical Characterization^{^{1}}\n\nT W Miller\n\n### T W Miller\n\n^{a}Merck Sharp & Dohme Research Laboratories, Rahway, New Jersey 07065\n\nFind articles by T W Miller\n\n^{a}, R T Goegelman\n\n### R T Goegelman\n\n^{a}Merck Sharp & Dohme Research Laboratories, Rahway, New Jersey 07065\n\nFind articles by R T Goegelman\n\n^{a}, R G Weston\n\n### R G Weston\n\n^{a}Merck Sharp & Dohme Research Laboratories, Rahway, New Jersey 07065\n\nFind articles by R G Weston\n\n^{a}, I Putter\n\n### I Putter\n\n^{a}Merck Sharp & Dohme Research Laboratories, Rahway, New Jersey 07065\n\nFind articles by I Putter\n\n^{a}, F J Wolf\n\n### F J Wolf\n\n^{a}Merck Sharp & Dohme Research Laboratories, Rahway, New Jersey 07065\n\nFind articles by F J Wolf\n\n^{a}\n\n  * [Button: Author information]\n  * [Button: Copyright and License information]\n\n^{a}Merck Sharp & Dohme Research Laboratories, Rahway, New Jersey 07065\n\n^{1}\n\nPresented in part at the 11th Interscience Conference on Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy, Atlantic City, N.J., 19–22 October 1971.\n\nCopyright © 1972 American Society for Microbiology\n\nPMC Copyright notice\n\nPMCID: PMC444279  PMID: 4790553\n\n## Abstract\n\nCephamycins A and B were isolated from the same fermentation broth of various actinomycetes by adsorption and ion-exchange methods. The antibiotics were separated from each other by column chromatography on a dextran-based ion-exchange resin. Cephamycin C was isolated from a different fermentation broth by ion-exchange and gel-filtration methods. The chemical characteristics of these new antibiotics were determined.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProduct Information (https://www.himedialabs.com/media/TD/GRM1365.pdf)\nciteturn26search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; Ammonium metavanadate ... 7803-55-6 ... NH₄VO₃\nProduct Information \nProduct Information \n \n \nRevision :    02\n \nDate of Revision: 11.09.2024 \nAmmonium metavanadate \nGRM1365 \nProduct Identifier \nCAS No. \n: \n7803-55-6 \nEC No. \n: \n232-261-3 \nMolecular Formula \n: \nNH₄VO₃ \nMolecular Weight \n: \n116.98 \nHS Code \n: \n2841 90 00 \nStorage \n: \nBelow 30°C \nShelf life \n: \n  4 years \n \n \n \n \nTechnical Specification \nAppearance \n: White to pale green or tan crystals or powder or solid  \nSolubility \n: \n33.3 mg soluble in 1 mL of cooled mixture of \nwater : sulphuric acid(150:50) \nChloride (Cl) \n: \n<= 0.2% \nSulfate (SO₄) \n: \n<= 0.05% \nAssay (FAS Titration) \n: \nmin. 98.00% \n \nSafety Information \n \nHazard Pictogram(s) \n: \nSignal Word \n: Danger \nHazard Statement(s) \n: H301- H315- H319- H330- H335 \nPrecautionary Statement(s) \n: P260- P280- P284- P301 + P310- P304 + P340- P501 \nUN No. \n: 2859 \nClass \n: 6.1 \nPacking Group \n: II \nRTECS \n: YW0875000 \nWGK \n: 3 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nAddress : C-40, Road No.21/Y, MIDC, Wagle Ind. Area, Thane(W) - 400604, Maharashtra, India. Phone:+91-022-6147 1919, 6903 48 00  \nFax:+91-022-6147 1920,6903 48 90  email : info@himedialabs.com. Visit us at our website: www.himedialabs.com \nThe information contained herein is believed to be accurate and complete. However no warranty or guarantee whatsoever is made or is to be implied with \nrespect to such Information or with respect to any product, method or apparatus referred to herein------------------------------